{"name":"Wildflower Prairie","hex":"#cccfe2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wildflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild (uncultivated) flowering plant.","A flower from such a plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wildflower"},{"term":"prairie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extensive area of relatively flat grassland with few, if any, trees, especially in North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prairie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wildflower","blocks":[{"text":"A wildflower is a flower that grows in the wild, rather than being intentionally seeded or planted. The term implies that the plant is neither a hybrid nor a selected cultivar that is any different from the native plant, even if it is growing where it would not naturally be found. The term can refer to the whole plant, even when not in bloom, and not just the flower."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/DwSixspecies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildflower","wikidata":"Q3585615"},{"title":"Prairie","blocks":[{"text":"Prairies are ecosystems considered part of the temperate grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome by ecologists, based on similar temperate climates, moderate rainfall, and a composition of grasses, herbs, and shrubs, rather than trees, as the dominant vegetation type. Temperate grassland regions include the Pampas of Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay, and the steppe of Romania, Ukraine, Russia, and Kazakhstan. Lands typically referred to as \"prairie\" tend to be in North America. The term encompasses the lower and mid-latitude of the area referred to as the Interior Plains of Canada, the United States, and Mexico. It includes all of the Great Plains as well as the wetter, hillier land to the east. From west to east, generally the drier expanse of shortgrass prairie gives way to mixed grass prairie and ultimately the richer and wetter soils of the tallgrass prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg/330px-James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prairie","wikidata":"Q194281"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wildflowers of Western Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWildflowers_western_australia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png/500px-Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png/1280px-Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png/500px-Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlieb_wikimedia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wildflowers are blooming in April in a field in central Texas near Lake Grapevine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrassland_S